The K-map shows `out = 0` only for the minterm where `a=0, b=0, c=0` (bc=00, a=0); all other cells are 1. Grouping the 1s gives the three groups `a`, `b`, and `c`, so `out = a | b | c`. The module compiles cleanly.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input  wire a,
    input  wire b,
    input  wire c,
    output wire out
);

    // K-map: out is 0 only for minterm (a=0, b=0, c=0)
    // Groups: a, b, c  =>  out = a | b | c
    assign out = a | b | c;

endmodule
```
